# Local docs clone (~400MB). Cloned on request by the `/sn-init` SKILL (the agent, not the
# script — scripts/sn-init never clones). Refresh: `git -C vendor/ServiceNowDocs pull`.
vendor/

# SDK build artifacts — regenerate with `now-sdk build`.
# Fluent projects are not only under apps/: the loop builds in place under
# enhancements/<number>/, and one of those was 544MB of node_modules. Match anywhere.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/target/
**/.npm-cache/

# THE LINE: what ships is what a stranger can RUN. What stays is what only makes sense
# to us — anything derived from our instance, our tickets, or our run history. See
# CLAUDE.md § What ships and what stays. Every rule below is one instance of that line.

# Evidence is a receipt taken by one operator against one instance. It cannot be
# verified by anyone else, it goes stale the moment the thing it describes changes, and
# a stale receipt is worse than no receipt in a repo whose whole pitch is "never trust a
# success message". Directory-wide, at any depth, so a future app inherits the rule
# instead of needing its own line.
**/evidence/

# Per-enhancement working output: real tickets, real business-unit content, our specs
# and packages. The loop CONTRACT ships (the skills read it); the tickets never do.
enhancements/*
!enhancements/loop.md

# Fluent apps built to DELIVER an enhancement. The rig's own apps ship — a stranger can
# install them on their instance and they do something. A ticket's app cannot: it is
# wired to our sys_ids (our business applications, our users, our groups, our vendors),
# so on anyone else's instance it is a pile of dangling references. Same line as
# enhancements/* — the contract ships, the ticket never does.
#
# Allowlist, not blocklist, deliberately: the next enhancement scaffolds an app nobody
# remembers to add a rule for, and the default has to be "stays" or that app is the hole.
# Adding a rig app is one line here, and that line is a decision someone made on purpose.
apps/*
!apps/ai-development-control-plane/

# Run journals, by name, anywhere. These are the arc, not the product.
**/BUILD_JOURNAL.md
**/NEXT_AGENT_PROMPT.md

# Documents the requester attached to the ticket. The loop downloads them here and reads
# them; they belong to the business unit that sent them, not to this repo. Read in place,
# never commit. This is the recipient's confidential material, not ours.
**/handoff-in/

# Never. Credentials live in ~/.snpdi/env, outside the repo entirely.
.env*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
.snpdi

# Generated grounding — every instance generates its own via /sn-map; never shipped.
codex/instance-profile.md
__pycache__/

# Working state of the current build-out — lives with the experiment's own record, not in
# the shipped product. A fresh clone starts with CLAUDE.md and the codex, not our head-state.
HEAD_STATE.md
data/
.agents/


# Recording leftovers
*.cast
*.orig
.DS_Store
